# Allow records for scripts/ablation/check-public-content.sh, one deferral
# per record rather than a silence. The format, the closed set of
# allowlistable classes, and the self-scan that keeps a record from carrying
# what the check refuses are documented in that script's header.
#
# Format, tab-separated, four fields:
#
#   <class-id>  <file>  <issue>  <reason>
#
# A record covers one file for one class. It is a deliberate decision on the
# record: the file legitimately holds the literal, the reason says why, and
# the issue tracks the deferral.

wip-path	scripts/check-template-directives_test.sh	tsukumogami/shirabe#738	The lint's own fixtures: one gate script names the parent state path to test the publish carve-out, one invoked script reads a child staging file to test that the staging-folder limb binds gate commands only. The literals are the subject under test.
wip-path	skills/scope/scripts/resume-probe_test.sh	tsukumogami/shirabe#738	The probe's seeds: the suite writes the old state and handoff files to prove the session-era probe no longer reads them. Reviewers and cleanup steps grep committed code for staging paths, and an assembled or hidden form would defeat them, so the literals stay visible.
